#: RMSD.md:1
msgid "RMSD and PCAVARS"
msgstr "RMSD と PCAVARS"

#: RMSD.md:3
msgid ""
"One of the things that has bothered me for some time RMSD. RMSD is used in "
"many different methods. Furthermore, in many of these methods the RMSD can "
"be replaced with a simple Eudlidean distance that is calculated by taking "
"the difference between two sets of argument values. For these methods I "
"always wanted to write one impelementation that would work with both RMSD "
"and Euclidean distances. However, I feel like the impelementations of these "
"things that I wrote in the past were always an overcomplicated mess. I now "
"think that I have written something simpler that still provides the same "
"flexibility. I would like to explain how this works by discussing how "
"PCAVARS are implemented."
msgstr ""
"RMSD は多手法で使い、しばしば引数間の Euclidean Distance "
"に置換できます。両方を単一実装で扱いたかったのですが、従来は複雑すぎました。同じ柔軟性で単純化した方法を PCAVARS で説明します。"

#: RMSD.md:8
msgid ""
"Before getting into the code lets first briefly recap the theory. When you "
"calculate a PCA variable you are essentially projecting a vector connecting "
"the instantaneous configuration to some reference configuration on to a "
"reference vector. In other words, a PCA variable is computed by taking the a"
" dot product like this"
msgstr "PCA は瞬時と参照の変位 Vector を参照 Vector に射影する Dot Product です。"

#: RMSD.md:15
msgid ""
"where $v_i$ represents the components of the reference vector, $x_i$ is the "
"instantenous position and $y_i$ is the reference position. When this is done"
" with RMSD you do an alignment (i.e. a removal of translation and rotation "
"of atoms) before calculating the $(x_i - y_i)$ values by calculating how far"
" each position has moved relative to the reference structure."
msgstr ""
"$v_i$ は参照 Vector、$x_i$ は瞬時位置、$y_i$ は参照位置です。RMSD では回転・並進を除き、$(x_i - y_i)$ "
"を求めます。"

